<title>USA: LTV shares recommended - Barron's.</title>
<headline>LTV shares recommended - Barron's.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of LTV Corp may be a strong buy now, with its bankruptcy and nearly seven years of restructuring behind it, according to Barron's.</p>
<p>The company, whose shares closed at 12-1/2 Friday, came out of Chapter 11 in 1993 and now has about $6-per share in cash and is practically debt-free, the magazine said.</p>
<p>The company is also the only integrated steel producer in the U.S. in the mini-mill business, Barron's added.</p>
<p>Said John Neff, a Barron's roundtable panelist who recently ran the Vanguard group's Windsor Fund, &quot;The company is in good shape and I can see them out in the future earning a couple bucks a share.&quot;</p>
<p>LTV earned $1.01 per share for 1996.</p>
</text>
